TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
SUMMARY:e-Energy 2027: Abstract registration (fall deadline) (23:59 AoE)
DESCRIPTION:ACM International Conference on Future and Sustainable Energy S
 ystems (e-Energy 2027)\n\nAbstract registration (fall deadline): 11 Sept 2
 026\, 23:59 AoE\n\nConference: June 5-11\, 2027\nLocation: Atlanta\, USA\n
 Venue: Hyatt Regency Atlanta\n\nAll dates:\n  Abstract registration (fall 
 deadline): 11 Sept 2026\, 23:59 AoE\n  Paper submission (fall deadline): 1
 8 Sept 2026\, 23:59 AoE\n  Test of Time Award nomination submission: 15 Oc
 t 2026\, 23:59 AoE\n  Author notification (fall deadline): 6 Nov 2026\, 23
 :59 UTC+12 (assumed)\n  Revision submission (fall deadline): 20 Nov 2026\,
  23:59 AoE\n  Revision notification (fall deadline): 10 Dec 2026\, 23:59 U
 TC+12 (assumed)\n  Abstract registration (winter deadline): 8 Jan 2027\, 2
 3:59 AoE\n  Paper submission (winter deadline): 15 Jan 2027\, 23:59 AoE\n 
  Author notification (winter deadline): 5 Mar 2027\, 23:59 UTC+12 (assumed
 )\n  Revision submission (winter deadline): 19 Mar 2027\, 23:59 AoE\n  Rev
 ision notification (winter deadline): 16 Apr 2027\, 23:59 UTC+12 (assumed)
 \n  Camera-ready due (both deadlines): 30 Apr 2027\, 23:59 AoE\n\nThe call
  for papers states no timezone. This is counted as UTC+12\, the earliest i
 t could plausibly mean\, so the countdown runs out before the real deadlin
 e rather than after it.\n\n18th edition\, part of the inaugural ACM Sustai
 nability Week and co-located with ACM FCRC 2027. Two submission rounds\, f
 all and winter\; the fall round is recommended for authors facing long vis
 a processing. Each HotCRP site opens three weeks before its deadline. Full
  papers are up to 10 pages and Notes papers up to 4 pages (9-point ACM sig
 conf\, double-column\, excluding references and appendices)\, double-blind
 . Full papers may be accepted\, rejected or asked to revise\; the camera-r
 eady version gets one extra page. Authors choose one of four tracks (Contr
 ol and energy systems\, Learning\, Systems and applied modeling\, Theory).
  Selected rejected full papers may be invited as Notes papers. Papers reje
 cted in the fall round may not be resubmitted in the winter round. Accepte
 d papers from both rounds must be presented in June 2027. Proceedings are 
 open access\; authors from institutions outside ACM Open pay a subsidised 
 APC of $250 (ACM/SIG members) or $350. The ACM Digital Library publication
  date\, which matters for patent filings\, may be up to two weeks before t
 he conference. Notification dates state no time or timezone.\n\nCall for p
 apers: https://energy.acm.org/conferences/eenergy/2027/\nDetails: https://
 powersystemdeadlines.org/preview/pr-16/conference/e-energy27
LOCATION:Atlanta\, USA
URL;VALUE=URI:https://eenergy27fall.hotcrp.com
CATEGORIES:Smart Grid,Computation & Optimization,Energy Markets,Renewables
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SEQUENCE:0
